 "drivingQuestion": "What is the 'green moss' of the mishna?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "Rav Pappa's identification (ship moss) stands after the standing-water candidate is rejected",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "shabbat.20b.12",
   "daf": "20b",
   "sentenceId": 11,
   "he": "וְלֹא בִּירוֹקָה שֶׁעַל כּוּ׳. מַאי הִיא? אִילֵימָא אוּכַּמְתָּא דַחֲרִיצֵי — אִיפָּרוֹכֵי מִפָּרְכָן. אֶלָּא אָמַר רַב פָּפָּא: אוּכַּמְתָּא דְּאַרְבָּא.",
   "en": "«And» we learned in the mishna that «one may not» use the «green» moss «that is on» the surface of the water to fashion a wick for lighting the Shabbat lamp. The Gemara asks: «What is this» green moss? «If you say» that it is the «moss found on standing water,» isn’t that moss «brittle» and therefore unfit material from which to fashion a wick? «Rather, Rav Pappa said:» It is referring to «the moss» that accumulates «on ships,» which is more pliable and when dried can be fashioned into a wick."
  }
 ],
